// Praxis v0 standard prelude — inert reference template.
//
// ABI DECISIONS (see also mesh/test/praxis-examples-v0.test.mjs and PR body):
// 1. The prelude may name ONLY what the analyzer already pins as authority
//    kinds: permit, lease, quorum, secret, prepared. It declares the five
//    `requires` forms below as the canonical naming template.
// 2. It binds NO host symbols. host-symbols.mjs exports JS-level Symbols
//    (HOST_AUTHORITY, HOST_SECRET_REF, HOST_PREPARED_REF, ...). Those live in
//    the synthetic test host's runtime registries and are NOT addressable in
//    v0 Praxis syntax. The prelude therefore references no host symbol and
//    claims no host capability.
// 3. Policies (verify/assess `with` names) and provenance strings are
//    unbound in v0: the language carries the names but enforces nothing
//    about them. The registry conventions below are PROVISIONAL and are
//    enforced, if at all, by hosts off-language.
// 4. Secret kinds, action names, and scope names are opaque words in v0.
//    The vocabularies used below (e.g. `api_key`, `Operate @ Mesh`) are
//    PROVISIONAL fixtures; a host capability contract must pin them before
//    any non-lab use.
// 5. The prelude is a TEMPLATE, not a module: v0 has no import mechanism,
//    and prepending these declarations to a program that redeclares the
//    same names would fail with PRAXIS_DUPLICATE_BINDING. Copy-and-rename,
//    or wait for a module system (PROVISIONAL).
// 6. This file must itself pass `node cli.mjs check` and
//    `node cli.mjs format --check`; comments survive here because the
//    formatter strips them on re-emit — this file is documentation, not
//    gallery input, so it is NOT held to the examples' comment-free rule.

// Standard authority declarations. Rename the binding names to fit the
// program that needs them; keep the form and the action @ scope shape.
requires permit standard_ops: Operate @ Mesh;
requires lease burst_window: Burst @ Compute;
requires quorum change_board: Approve @ Ledger threshold 2 of alice, bob;
requires secret service_token: api_key;
requires prepared nightly_snapshot: Snapshot @ Backups;

// PROVISIONAL — policy name registry conventions (v0: unenforced).
// Hosts that consume `with <Policy>` names are expected to publish the set
// they recognize. These fixtures exist only to give examples a stable
// vocabulary; they grant nothing by themselves.
